A poor couple each secretly sells their most treasured possession to buy a Christmas gift for the other, leaving both gifts unusable yet proving their love the wisest of all.

1. Poor Love Two Treasures  (passages 1-2)
    A poor young wife desperate to honor her husband at Christmas cherishes their two proud
    possessions before rushing out with a sudden resolve.
       -> Her lack of money and longing for a worthy gift push her to sacrifice something
       precious to pay for one.
2. Selling Hair for Chain  (passages 3-3)
    She cuts and sells her long hair to buy a fine platinum chain for her husband's heirloom
    watch.
       -> Having changed her looks and bought the chain, she must now go home and face how her
       husband will see her.
3. Anxious Wait and Stare  (passages 4-4)
    Back home with short curls she waits nervously, fears she looks less pretty, and explains
    her sacrifice when her husband stares in shock.
       -> Her fear and his strange unreadable stare demand an explanation, so he must struggle
       to understand and answer her.
4. Reassurance and Surprise Gift  (passages 5-5)
    He insists his love is unchanged by her haircut and gives her a package that first delights
    her and then makes her cry.
       -> Her swing from joy to tears over his mysterious package leaves its meaning unsolved
       until the final reveal explains both gifts.
5. Useless Gifts Wisest Love  (passages 6-6)
    Both gifts prove unusable because he sold his watch to buy her combs, which the story
    celebrates as the wisest kind of giving.
